      en: "Tufton Hall Waterfall is a 15-meter cascade located in northeastern Grenada, near the village of Tivoli. Fed by the Balthazar River, the waterfall plunges into a natural pool surrounded by lush rainforest. The area is a biodiversity hotspot, home to many bird species such as the Grenada dove and tropical flora. The waterfall is accessible via a short hiking trail that takes about 20 minutes through the forest. Local farmers maintain the path and offer fresh produce. The best time to visit is during the rainy season from June to December when the water flow is strongest. The pool is suitable for swimming, but caution is advised after heavy rainfall.",
